<title>UK: GECC sets $300 million seven-year bond.</title>
<headline>GECC sets $300 million seven-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager ABN AMRO Hoare Govett and Paribas.</p>
<p> BORROWER   GENERAL ELECTRIC CAPITAL CORP</p>
<p> AMT    $300 MLN	COUPON     6.25	MATURITY    18.AUG.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.075   PAY DATE    18.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.50     SPREAD	+17 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  U.S.	TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.30	SELL CONC  1.575     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND JULY 2002 U.S. TREASURY NOTE  NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME, NOT 144A</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
